<Step id="STEP_6_EMIT_HANDOFF">
      <Goal>Close the phase block with a typed Handoff and DONE.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Append `<ts> DONE` via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> line "DONE" --phase <PhaseID>`; append the
        `**Handoff →**` line via `npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> handoff "<payload>" --phase <PhaseID>` per
        `HANDOFF_FORMAT` (typed payload,
        `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` — the tool is the sole writer for both lines, never
        a manual `Edit`, and this phase's OWN and ONLY write of them — the orchestrator that dispatched
        this phase reads this Handoff line back but never re-logs it, per its own logging-zone boundary)
        — its `deviations:` field lists the id of every Decision Log entry this phase
        added while self-resolving a ticket gap (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`; empty `[]` when none);
        flip this phase's Status in Phases Overview `[ ]` → `[x]` via a direct `Edit`
        (outside the Execution Log, `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE`); return the structured summary per
        `RETURN_SUMMARY_FORMAT` to the orchestrator.
      </Action>
    </Step>

<Axiom id="AX_HANDOFF_TYPED">
      End every phase block with a typed Handoff line consumed by the next phase and the orchestrator. Format per `HANDOFF_FORMAT`. Free-form text forbidden — the next phase reads keys, not narrative.
    </Axiom>

<Contract id="HANDOFF_FORMAT">
      Compact, typed, single line at end of phase block:
      ```
      **Handoff →** artifacts: [path1, path2]; decisions: [key=value, key=value]; open: [id: text, id: text]; deviations: [id: text, id: text]
      ```
      Fields:
      - `artifacts` — files produced or modified by this phase (paths).
      - `decisions` — key facts the next phase or audit needs (e.g. `IdempotencyKey=introduced`, `module-system=esm`).
      - `open` — unresolved questions / risks / deferred sub-tasks (id + one-line). Empty list → `[]`.
      - `deviations` — spec/ticket holes this phase self-resolved rather than asking the operator
        (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`); each entry cites the ticket-local Decision Log id it produced
        (e.g. `TSK-58-D-2: chose retry cap 3, spec silent on it`). Empty list → `[]`.

      Free-form text forbidden. Each field is an array (possibly empty).
    </Contract>

<Contract id="RETURN_SUMMARY_FORMAT">
      JSON-like return to orchestrator:
      ```
      {
        "status": "DONE" | "BLOCKED" | "FAIL",
        "task_id": "<TSK-NN>",
        "phase_id": "<P<N>>",
        "kind": "<kind>",
        "artifacts": ["<path>", ...],
        "decisions": ["<key=value>", ...],
        "open": ["<id: text>", ...],
        "deviations": ["<id: text>", ...],
        "blocker_reason": "<if BLOCKED>"
      }
      ```
      `artifacts` / `decisions` / `open` / `deviations` mirror the **Handoff →** line — orchestrator
      threads `artifacts` / `decisions` / `open` into the next phase's prompt, and collects
      `deviations` across the run for the end-of-cycle batched report (`AX_DEVIATION_SELF_RESOLVE`).
    </Contract>